This repository contains the submission materials for "Rare Disease, Real Kid: The MVA Hackathon 2026",
organised by Sage Bionetworks with the MVA Society, Hugging Face and BEACON.

WHAT THIS LICENCE COVERS
    The original work in this repository: the analysis code (scripts/), the reports and figures (reports/),
    the documentation (docs/) and the research notes (research_notes/).

    You are free to share and adapt this material for any purpose, including commercially, provided you give
    appropriate credit, link to the licence, and indicate if changes were made.

    Full licence text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode
    Summary:           https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

WHAT THIS LICENCE DOES NOT COVER
    The Hackathon dataset. The genomic and clinical data of the child are controlled-access material
    (WCG IRB protocol #20252010), governed by the Hackathon Rules and the Data Transfer Agreement. They are
    NOT contained in this repository and are NOT redistributed under this licence. They are deleted within 30 days
    after the Hackathon closes, as the terms require.

    Files in this repository that are not original work:
      - reports/latex/fonts/ — IBM Plex fonts, SIL Open Font License 1.1 (reports/latex/fonts/OFL.txt);
      - docs/methods_description_form.xlsx and docs/track1_submission_template.csv — templates provided by the
        hackathon organisers;
      - fields taken from ChEMBL in reports/t2/*.csv and *.md (molecule identifiers, phases, mechanisms) —
        ChEMBL data are CC BY-SA 3.0.

    Third-party components, each under its own terms. In particular, AlphaMissense predictions are CC BY-NC-SA
    4.0 and were used here under their non-commercial terms; ClinVar, gnomAD, Ensembl, UniProt, ChEMBL,
    openFDA, LINCS, Exomiser and the other public resources cited in the reports keep their own licences.

ACKNOWLEDGEMENT
    This work was made possible through the Hackathon, organized by Sage Bionetworks in partnership with the
    MVA Society, Hugging Face, and BEACON (The Benchmarking, Evaluation, and Assessment Consortium for
    Science), with prize sponsorship from AWS and Anthropic. We are deeply grateful to the child and their
    family who generously contributed their data and their story to advance research into this rare disease.
    We acknowledge their trust in making this Hackathon possible.

NOT MEDICAL ADVICE
    Everything here is a research hypothesis for a clinical team to evaluate. Nothing in this repository is
    medical advice, a diagnosis, or evidence that any medicine works in mosaic variegated aneuploidy.
